## F. P2 — RESEARCH, SOURCES, SAFETY, RIGHTS

- [ ] **MW-RSC-01 / Corpus** — Only activate Scripture module after source/edition/license-provenance schema, independently sourced sample fixtures and API tests. **DoD:** text attribution, edition, language, translation, license always visible.
- [ ] **MW-RSC-02 / Research** — Link MoonWitness story/episode to existing ResearchRun evidence IDs without silently merging fiction, interpretation and empirical observations. **DoD:** citation card shows claim type and verifiable source.
- [ ] **MW-RSC-03 / Mizan** — Implement review field for claim, supporting/opposing sources, uncertainty, corrections, editorial sign-off. **DoD:** factual errors can be corrected with revision note.
- [ ] **MW-RSC-04 / Naming** — Clarify `ZIIL` safeguarding module versus **ZILL** Tasawuf/Tarekat editorial collection to avoid namespace and theological confusion. **DoD:** distinct slugs and copy.
- [ ] **MW-RSC-05 / Privacy** — Consent for real-person testimony, redaction, minors and sensitive locations; separate symbolic characters from real operators. **DoD:** redaction controls effective after publication.
- [ ] **MW-RSC-06 / Copyright** — For music-related episodes, avoid unlicensed full lyrics, album artwork and third-party figures; record licensing/attribution. **DoD:** rights checklist on every published multimedia episode.
- [ ] **MW-RSC-07 / Safeguarding** — Review religious-comparison pages for careful attribution: what scripture actually says versus a user's symbolic reading. **DoD:** classification and source provenance visible.
- [ ] **MW-RSC-08 / Governance** — Require written ADR and approval before using this monorepo to replace MoonWitness Gen2's canonical data/API. **DoD:** boundaries, rollback and compatibility tests signed off.
- [ ] **MW-RSC-09 / Registry** — Treat Asma/DNA 99 and V5 physics research as metadata/proposals, not deployed capabilities. **DoD:** UI labels and APIs avoid false operational claims.

