**Creative invariant:** Keep MoonWitness logotype visually dominant, Empire of the Light / A-L-L-A-H as parent endorsement, SHADOW the operator sub-brand. Palette: #050505 / #FF168F / #0787FF / #FFE500 / #F7F1E7 as reference art-direction values (map through approved UI design tokens); faceless hoodies, large blue moon, ripped-paper collage, 2D comic panels, manga speed lines, photocopy grain. Public portal expressive; editor surfaces operational and readable. Do not copy poster lyrics or copyrighted art as page assets without rights.

## Suggested milestone order & dependencies

1. **M0 CI green:** MW-P0-01..09; tests/build, only then branch promotion. **Blocked currently**.
2. **M1 Secure deploy:** MW-P0-10..15 + OPS-01..09; verify public/secret boundary before advertising site.
3. **M2 Content MVP:** DATA-01..16 + PUB-02/03/04/07 + SHD-10/11/12; a single real story publishes end-to-end.
4. **M3 Creative production:** SHD-02..09, PUB-05/06/08..10; coherent creator-to-reader product.
5. **M4 Research & governance:** RSC-01..09 + NFR-01..09; evidence- and rights-governed releases.
6. **M5 Expanded universe:** advanced analytics, collaborations, richer graph, optional AI-assisted poster generation behind approved adapters.

### End-to-end acceptance scenario — single vertical slice

1. Authorized writer creates Collection `moonwitness`, Story `tick-tock-on-the-clock`, Episode 001, and two ComicPages in SHADOW.
2. Writer attaches two original media assets, alt text, a personal-testimony classification, and a source link.
3. Editor requests review; independent authorized reviewer approves; publisher schedules or publishes revision R1.
4. Guest visits `/`, opens Universe → collection → episode, reads page 1→2 and navigates back without logging in.
5. Dashboard counts exactly one published episode; draft content remains invisible to guest and other tenant.
6. Authorized editor corrects copy in R2 without overwriting R1 until approved; revision and decision are auditable.
7. Publisher unpublishes; public cache invalidates; archived content disappears from listing but audit remains available privately.
8. Backup/restoration preserves R1/R2, assets, source attribution and access controls.

